;;; subject: opendev-terminal-agent-2603 2.3.7 Context Retrieval and Assembly Pipeline: how the code the agent needs is found by tools of rising cost and put together with instructions and history within the token budget
;;; made-from: doc_Base012/docs/Papers-AgentHarness/opendev-terminal-agent/03_context-engineering/03_context-engineering.lisp / s29 .. s34
;;; members: importance layer1 layer2 layer3 layer4 flow next
;;; elsewhere: none
;;; left-out: the caption of Figure 15 and the closing sentence that leads to the next section is kept as the last member
(defrule retrieval -> retrieval-importance retrieval-layer1 retrieval-layer2 retrieval-layer3 retrieval-layer4 retrieval-flow retrieval-next)
(defrule retrieval-importance -> :nucleus retrieval-importance/n :elaboration-additional retrieval-importance/a1 :elaboration-additional retrieval-importance/a2 :elaboration-additional retrieval-importance/a3 :elaboration-additional retrieval-importance/a4)
(defrule retrieval-importance/n -> :instruction "探索の質が以後の行動の質を決めることを 1 文で書く" :sample "Context retrieval is the single most consequential capability of a coding agent: the quality of every downstream action (editing, testing, planning) is bounded by whether the agent has located the right code in the first place.")
(defrule retrieval-importance/a1 -> :instruction "従来の一回きりの検索の方式を 1 文で書く" :sample "In traditional RAG pipelines [41], retrieval is a static, one-shot operation: embed the query, fetch top- k documents, and generate.")
(defrule retrieval-importance/a2 -> :instruction "コードに対してそれが合わない理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "This works reasonably well for factual question answering over homogeneous corpora, but codebases are fundamentally different.")
(defrule retrieval-importance/a3 -> :instruction "探索を行動と交互に行う見方を 1 文で書く" :sample "Recent work on agentic search [85] has shown that effective retrieval in complex environments requires the agent to dynamically control when, what, and how to retrieve, interleaving reasoning with search rather than treating retrieval as a preprocessing step [96, 77].")
(defrule retrieval-importance/a4 -> :instruction "採った四つの層の流れを 1 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev instantiates this principle for software engineering through a four-layer pipeline (Figure 15) that progressively escalates from simple lookups to multi-step agentic search to full context assembly and optimization.")
(defrule retrieval-layer1 -> :nucleus retrieval-layer1/n :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer1/a1 :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer1/a2 :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer1/a3 :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer1/a4)
(defrule retrieval-layer1/n -> :instruction "探索の道具の種類を挙げて 1 文で書く" :sample "Five tools form the retrieval surface: read_file for targeted file access, list_files for glob-based discovery, text_search (ripgrep) for pattern matching, find_symbol for LSP-based semantic resolution, and ast_search (ast-grep) for structural pattern matching (Sections 2.4.2 and 2.4.5).")
(defrule retrieval-layer1/a1 -> :instruction "設計上の問いが道具の選び方であることを 1 文で書く" :sample "The central design question is not what tools to provide, but how the agent selects among them.")
(defrule retrieval-layer1/a2 -> :instruction "問いの中で最も強い手掛かりから道具を選ぶ原則を 1 文で書く" :sample "Effective retrieval instead begins by identifying the strongest anchor in the query: the most specific, highest-signal element that constrains the search space.")
(defrule retrieval-layer1/a3 -> :instruction "手掛かりの種類ごとの道具を 1 文で書く" :sample "Symbol names (e.g., AuthController.validate) route to find_symbol, which resolves the definition semantically via LSP; string literals and error messages route to text_search, which performs exact pattern matching; structural patterns (e.g., “all Python if-statements that check is_admin ”) route to ast_search, which matches language-aware templates; and file-path conventions route to list_files for glob-based discovery.")
(defrule retrieval-layer1/a4 -> :instruction "この原則の効果を 1 文で書く" :sample "By matching the retrieval tool to the anchor type, the agent avoids noisy, low-precision searches and reaches the relevant code in fewer steps.")
(defrule retrieval-layer2 -> :nucleus retrieval-layer2/n :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer2/a1 :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer2/a2 :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer2/a3)
(defrule retrieval-layer2/n -> :instruction "単独の道具で足りない探索を、別のエージェントに任せる流れを 1 文で書く" :sample "Single-tool retrieval suffices when the agent knows exactly what to look for, but many tasks require exploratory retrieval: the agent must follow cross-references, discover unexpected dependencies, and iteratively narrow a broad search space.")
(defrule retrieval-layer2/a1 -> :instruction "任せる先と、その持つ道具を 1 文で書く" :sample "When the main agent needs broad codebase understanding rather than a pinpoint lookup, it delegates to the Code Explorer subagent (Sections 2.2.7 and 2.4.8), which runs in an isolated context window with access to the same five retrieval tools in read-only mode.")
(defrule retrieval-layer2/a2 -> :instruction "任された側の探索の進め方を 1 文で書く" :sample "The subagent performs multi-step searches autonomously: it might start with find_symbol to locate a class definition, read the file to discover its dependencies, then use text_search to trace how those dependencies are used across the project.")
(defrule retrieval-layer2/a3 -> :instruction "文脈を分ける重要さを 1 文で書く" :sample "Context isolation is critical: intermediate search results (potentially thousands of lines of code) stay in the subagent’s window, and only the distilled summary is returned to the main agent.")
(defrule retrieval-layer3 -> :nucleus retrieval-layer3/n :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer3/a1 :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer3/a2 :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer3/a3)
(defrule retrieval-layer3/n -> :instruction "探した結果だけでは足りず、何を組み合わせるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Retrieved code artifacts alone are insufficient; the agent also needs its behavioral instructions, accumulated experience, and conversation history.")
(defrule retrieval-layer3/a1 -> :instruction "組み上げる材料の数と順を 1 文で書く" :sample "Before each model call, ContextPicker assembles the final message list from six ordered sources: (1) the system prompt augmented with selected playbook strategies from the adaptive memory (Section 2.3.6), (2) project-level and user-level persistent rules, (3) inline @file references and image blocks supplied by the user, (4) the conversation history retrieved from SessionManager, (5) system reminders injected at the point of decision (Section 2.3.4), and (6) the current user query.")
(defrule retrieval-layer3/a2 -> :instruction "材料の出どころの記録を 1 文で書く" :sample "Each piece of context is wrapped in a ContextPiece that tracks its provenance (source subsystem, priority, token cost), enabling downstream components to make informed retention decisions when the budget is tight.")
(defrule retrieval-layer3/a3 -> :instruction "組み上がった構造の検証と修復を 1 文で書く" :sample "The assembled structure is validated by ValidatedMessageList, which enforces structural integrity (every assistant message with tool calls must be followed by matching tool results before the next user turn) and auto-repairs violations with synthetic error placeholders rather than failing outright.")
(defrule retrieval-layer4 -> :nucleus retrieval-layer4/n :elaboration-additional retrieval-layer4/a1)
(defrule retrieval-layer4/n -> :instruction "組み上げた文脈が段階的な圧縮を通ることを 1 文で書く" :sample "The assembled context passes through ContextCompactor for token-budget enforcement before entering the ReAct reasoning loop.")
(defrule retrieval-layer4/a1 -> :instruction "見積もりの基準を 1 文で書く" :sample "Token budgets are calibrated against API-reported prompt_tokens from the previous turn rather than local estimates, correcting for provider-side injections (safety preambles, tool schemas) that are invisible to the client.")
(defrule retrieval-flow -> :nucleus retrieval-flow/n :elaboration-additional retrieval-flow/a1)
(defrule retrieval-flow/n -> :instruction "四つの層が段階的に強まる流れをなぞることを 1 文で書く" :sample "The four layers form a retrieval pipeline that mirrors the escalation pattern seen in agentic search systems [85]: simple queries resolve at Layer 1 with a single tool call; complex queries escalate to Layer 2’s multi-step search; all results converge at Layer 3’s assembly; and Layer 4 enforces the token budget.")
(defrule retrieval-flow/a1 -> :instruction "簡単な探索と広い探索の費用の違いを 1 文で書く" :sample "This progressive escalation means that straightforward lookups (“read file X”) incur minimal overhead, while open-ended exploration (“how does the authentication system work?”) can leverage the full agentic search loop without the cost bleeding into the main agent’s context.")
(defrule retrieval-next -> :nucleus retrieval-next/n)
(defrule retrieval-next/n -> :instruction "この層が決めるものと、次の層が決めるものを対にして 1 文で書く" :sample "The context engineering layer shapes what the model sees; the tool system defines what the model can do: the concrete actions through which the agent modifies code, runs commands, and interacts with the development environment.")
